note.p:
Overall, the primary contact is assumed to be James due to his involvement in Godwin's circle (see DNB  entry for James); 
      because the contacts continue after John's death; 
    and because 'John Tobin' is distinguished in 1803 but James is never distinguished. Godwin is not mentioned in
    Memoirs of John Tobin (1820). In addition, 
   a letter from Elizabeth Inchbald to Godwin which mentions the Tobins supports the above analysis.
